# Two divine feats reach the bearer's CARRIED GEAR, not just his hit points
# (bd inc-w26h).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/divine-feat-gear.keys 5
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. FT_DIVINE_RESISTANCE grants the bearer's Charisma
# modifier against fire, cold and lightning while he holds the CHANNELING
# stati, and FT_DIVINE_ARMOUR grants twice that modifier against five other
# types. src/Values.cpp reads both through one helper, DivineFeatResist, from
# BOTH Creature::ResistLevel (the bearer) and Creature::GearResistLevel (his
# equipment). This session asks one question: does the GEAR half reach a plain
# iron weapon?
#
# WHY THIS MEASURES DIVINE RESISTANCE AND NOT DIVINE ARMOUR. Of the five types
# Divine Armour covers, not one has a monster that can damage equipment with
# it: grep A_DEQU across lib/ and the damage types are fire, acid, decay, rust
# and shatter only. So Divine Armour has no live carrier to measure, and it is
# covered instead by the helper the two feats share plus the static rule in
# tools/equipment_static.py.
#
# WHY A FIREBAT. Its A_DEQU is 1d3 AD_FIRE with NO save DC (lib/mon2.irh:3716),
# and it is the only fire, cold or lightning carrier in lib/ with no DC. No DC
# matters: src/Fight.cpp:2122 sets e.ignoreHardness whenever a no-save A_DEQU
# strikes a NON-magical item, so iron contributes nothing at all and the feat's
# grant is the WHOLE of the number on the line.
#
# WHY CHARISMA 18, AND WHY THAT IS DECISIVE RATHER THAN LUCKY. The point-buy
# screen below spends all 75 points and puts Charisma at its 18 cap, so
# Creature::Mod returns (18-10)/2 = 4. Iron's fire hardness is 10 and the
# bypass zeroes it, so Item::Damage (src/Item.cpp:1480) computes hard = 0 + 4
# and then returns at :1544 whenever hard >= e.vDmg. 1d3 cannot exceed 3 and
# 4 > 3, so NO roll can reach the warhammer. Charisma 16 would also hold -- 3
# >= 3 returns too -- but only on the boundary, and 18 is one point clear of
# the largest roll the die has.
#
# HOW THE CHARACTER GETS CHANNELING. src/Skills.cpp:4492 grants
# CHANNELING for Charisma x 2 rounds whenever a character with any of seven
# divine feats uses Turn or Greater Turning. The grant is at :4492 and the turn
# is rolled at :4497, AFTER it, so the attempt does not have to succeed and no
# undead need be present: this session turns into an empty room and the game
# answers "You channel the sacred energies of Aiswin. Nothing happens." while
# still putting Channeling on the status line. What the code does require, all
# checked above the grant, is a god, that god's favour, and a holy symbol; a
# priest starts with all three. 36 rounds covers the whole session.
#
# WHY THE FEATS NEED A BUILT CHARACTER. src/FeatTab.cpp:630 asks
# FT_DIVINE_RESISTANCE for the Turning ability, Charisma 13 and FT_ENDURANCE,
# and FT_ENDURANCE (src/FeatTab.cpp:1215) asks Constitution 13. No rolled attribute set on
# this seed offers both, so the character is built at the point-buy screen
# instead of chosen from the five sets, and takes Endurance at one feat prompt
# and Divine Resistance at the next.
#
# WHY THIS SCRIPT CHANGES ONE SETTING, AND ONLY ONE. "Monsters Maximum Hit
# Points" is turned from NO to DOUBLE in the character generation options
# below. A firebat has 1 hit die, and a blow that KILLS its target leaves no
# item for the retaliation to aim at -- the engine aims it at the striker
# instead and prints "Fire sears you!", which is the same trap
# tools/keys/dequ-hardness-plain.keys describes. DOUBLE gives the bat
# 1 x d10 x 2, times 7/10 for being tiny (src/Values.cpp:2313), so 14 hit
# points; the warhammer below cannot roll past 12, so every fresh bat survives
# the blow that provokes it. Nothing else about the session changes.
#
# WHY A WARHAMMER. It is iron, mundane, an impact weapon the priest is
# proficient with, it rolls 1d8+4 = 5 to 12 which is under the bat's 14, and it
# has 45 hit points -- enough that the mutated run, which takes 1 to 3 points a
# blow, still has a page to read at the end.
#
# ONE BAT PER NEIGHBOURING SQUARE. Each bat survives its blow and stays where
# it is, so the next bat is summoned into the next of the eight squares round
# the character rather than into an occupied one. Every blow therefore lands on
# a fresh, off-guard bat.
#
# WHY A SEARCH TURN BEFORE EACH DUMP. The retaliation resolves after the screen
# the blow left behind, and the next blow's "Attack:" line overwrites the
# combat-numbers window before a dump can read it. One search costs a turn,
# starts no attack roll, and leaves the line standing:
#   "Warhammer: 1d3 Fire = 2 vs. 4 (iron) [unhurt]"
# With the gear grant taken out of GearResistLevel the same line reads
# "vs. 0 (iron)" and the hammer melts.

# --- a human priest, built to qualify, with Charisma at the point-buy cap ---
a                       # Create a New Character
y                       # Alter the character generation options -- yes
@until "everyone except your character" DOWN
@until "DOUBLE" SPACE   # Monsters Maximum Hit Points: NO -> DOUBLE
ESC
y                       # Explore Mode
@choose "Human"
@while "Choose a skill" a   # the two human bonus skills
@choose "Priest"
@choose "Aiswin"
p                       # Abort to Point Buy
RIGHT*10                # STR 18
DOWN RIGHT*6            # DEX 14
DOWN RIGHT*10           # CON 18 -- Endurance asks for 13
DOWN                    # INT  8
DOWN RIGHT*10           # WIS 18
DOWN RIGHT*10           # CHA 18 -- the number this check is about
DOWN RIGHT*5            # LUC 13; all 75 points are spent
ENTER y
a                       # Alignment: [a] Lawful Good
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@choose "Endurance"         # Divine Resistance cannot be taken before this
@choose "Divine Resistance"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y

# Freeze Monsters is the eleventh wizard switch. A frozen monster takes no turn
# of its own but still ANSWERS a blow, which is the whole point here.
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w y
w
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

# --- the weapon whose hit points are measured: an ordinary iron warhammer ---
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*9                 # walk the glyph row to ordinary weapons
@until "Warhammer" DOWN
DOWN                    # the wanted row is the middle of three; step onto it
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand
SPACE
@while "two-handed" n
s                       # stow the mace the swap pushed into the air
@until "Things in View" ESC

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
@until "base value of" x
@dump:divine-before
@until "Things in View" ESC

# Turn undead in an empty room. The grant is made before the roll.
@until "Use which skill" u
@choose "Turn Undead"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-channel

# The character sheet, as evidence that the feat is really held and that the
# grant is on the character at the magnitude the arithmetic needs.
d
@until "Resistances and Armour" DOWN
@dump:divine-sheet
@until "Things in View" ESC

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
RIGHT ENTER
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-01

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
PGDN ENTER
PGDN
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-02

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
DOWN ENTER
DOWN
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-03

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
END ENTER
END
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-04

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
LEFT ENTER
LEFT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-05

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
HOME ENTER
HOME
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-06

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
UP ENTER
UP
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-07

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "firebat"
PGUP ENTER
PGUP
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:divine-strike-08

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
@until "base value of" x
@dump:divine-after
@until "Things in View" ESC
@quit
